    "## 2. Prove the data matches the Mac copy\n",
    "A checksum is a fingerprint of a file. If these match, the test questions are exactly the ones used everywhere else, so scores are comparable. The cell stops with an error if they don't."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import json\n",
    "EXPECTED = {\n",
    "    \"train\": \"f8e91b1539abe869eb92f86800777b1fcd9cf802fe2c4153febabb6ea29d7b68\",\n",
    "    \"test\": \"2ac0aadeb3bc72bfc5e798fa916e1932306b47ac917bb0f2f7d96b703a4e75aa\",\n",
    "}\n",
    "manifest = json.load(open(\"data/manifest.json\"))\n",
    "for split, want in EXPECTED.items():\n",
    "    got = manifest[split][\"sha256\"]\n",
    "    assert got == want, f\"{split} checksum differs: {got}\"\n",
    "    print(split, manifest[split][\"rows\"], \"rows, checksum OK\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Baseline: score the untrained model\n",
    "This is the \"before\" number. The model gets the table design and a question, writes SQL, and each answer is run on a database and compared with the reference result.\n",
    "\n",
    "Start with a **20-question smoke test** (about a minute) to check everything works. Then run all **200** for the official baseline."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "MODEL = \"Qwen/Qwen2.5-Coder-0.5B-Instruct\"\n",
    "!python -m src.eval --model {MODEL} --limit 20 --out results/smoke"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "!python -m src.eval --model {MODEL} --out results/baseline"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Read the wrong answers\n",
    "Numbers say how often the model fails. Reading examples says why. Look for patterns: wrong column, extra text, a different but reasonable query."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import json, glob\n",
    "rows = [json.loads(l) for l in open(glob.glob(\"results/baseline/*.jsonl\")[0])]\n",
    "summary = json.load(open(glob.glob(\"results/baseline/*.summary.json\")[0]))\n",
    "print({k: summary[k] for k in (\"n\", \"execution_accuracy\", \"invalid_sql_rate\", \"uninformative_share\")})\n",
    "print(summary[\"failure_counts\"])\n",
    "bad = [r for r in rows if not r[\"correct\"]]\n",
    "for r in bad[:8]:\n",
    "    print(\"\\nQ   :\", r[\"question\"]); print(\"REF :\", r[\"reference\"]); print(\"PRED:\", r[\"predicted\"]); print(\"WHY :\", r[\"failure\"], \"|\", r[\"error\"])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Record the baseline\n",
    "Copy the numbers from section 4 into `notes.md` in the repo (on your Mac). This is the number the fine-tuned model must beat.\n",
